  "decisions": [
    {
      "concept": "arrival",
      "note": "LOAD's last homing move is the gear homing to the toolhead `filament_compression` switch (`extruder_homing_endstop: filament_compression`): 50 mm/s to endstop_pos 709.1 (= layout.extruder 700 + 9.1), then the extruder reverses off it. That is a plain toolhead switch -- no PSF analog, no buffer ramp -- so klipper-mmu's local toolhead switch input (`KLIPPER_MMU_PINS_TOOLHEAD`) can reproduce the sensing itself."
    },
    {
      "concept": "buffer_type",
      "note": "`[mmu_buffer unit0]` is a switched (tension/compression) buffer: `tension_pin: !unit0_buffer:PA1`, `compression_pin: !unit0_buffer:PA0`, `buffer_range 8`, `buffer_maxrange 13`, `buffer_spring_state: tension`. No proportional/PSF section. klipper-mmu carries switched buffer pins for follow (PINS_BUFFER_A/B) but no buffer ramming, so switched-buffer ramming is a gap, not a blocker."
    },
    {
      "concept": "encoder",
      "note": "`[mmu_unit unit0]` declares `encoder: unit0`, and KMS switches encoder checking on (`encoder_move_validation: 1`, `bowden_allowable_encoder_delta: 20.0`, `gate_endstop_to_encoder: 14`, `skip_cal_encoder: 1`). klipper-mmu's encoder input (`KLIPPER_MMU_ENCODER`) is optional and off by default for KMS, so the image runs without encoder checks; turning it on needs a wired `KLIPPER_MMU_PINS_ENCODER_A`."
    },
    {
      "concept": "espooler_assist",
      "note": "`[mmu_unit unit0]` also declares `espooler: unit0` (`espooler_operations: rewind, assist, print`, 100% burst power, `espooler_max_stepper_speed: 300`). Powered rewind is likewise optional (`KLIPPER_MMU_POWERED_REWIND`, off by default for KMS), so klipper-mmu's KMS runs without an espooler -- recorded as a gap."
    },
    {
      "concept": "preload_park",
      "note": "PRELOAD starts with a 300 mm homing move that ends ON `mmu_exit_0` (tip 0.0, 50 mm/s), then 'Final parking' pulls back 10 mm: `operations.preload.end.tip = -10.0` (`gate_preload_parking_distance: -10`). Rest position: 10 mm behind the gate exit switch. KMS is not in AFC, so there is no second number to weigh."
    },
    {
      "concept": "unload_park",
      "note": "`operations.unload.end.tip = -20.0` (`gate_parking_distance: -20`): the unload reverse-homes onto `mmu_exit_0` and parks 20 mm behind it. HH's number stands alone (KMS is not in AFC)."
    },
    {
      "concept": "eject_extra",
      "note": "EJECT asks for `gate_final_eject_distance: 300` but homes backwards, so it stops on the `mmu_entry` switch: `operations.eject.end.tip = -150.0` after only -130 mm of travel from the -20 park. The 300 mm budget is a ceiling; the entry switch is the real stop."
    }
  ]
}
